  $ sh repo-of.sh --help
    out: usage: sh repo-of.sh --dir FOLDER
    out: 
    out: Run by the domain's scripts; not for main to call.
    out: Names the repository FOLDER belongs to: the top folder of git's common
    out: directory, physical, which is its main checkout. A checkout and each of its
    out: worktrees name the same repository.
    out: 
    out: Options:
    out:   --dir FOLDER  a folder in a checkout or one of its worktrees, absolute
    out: Writes:    nothing
    out: Stdout:    one JSON line {repo, git_dir}: the main checkout's top folder and
    out:            its .git folder
    out: Exit:
    out:   0  named
    out:   2  refused, nothing changed; the reason is on stderr
    out:   3  FOLDER is in no git repository
    out:   4  git or jq not found
    out:   5  FOLDER's repository is bare: it has no checkout
