=== run-timed.sh: a command that ends within the limit
  $ sh run-timed.sh --seconds 5 -- sh -c echo to-stdout; echo to-stderr >&2; exit 7
    out: to-stdout
    err: to-stderr
    [exit 7]
  PASS: its stdout, its stderr and its own exit 7 pass through
  $ sh run-timed.sh --seconds 30 -- true
    [exit 0]
  PASS: a fast command returns at once with exit 0, not after the limit
  $ sh run-timed.sh --seconds 5 -- sh -c cat; echo read-to-end
    out: read-to-end
    [exit 0]
  PASS: stdin is closed: the command reads nothing
  $ sh run-timed.sh --seconds 1 -- sh -c exit 0
    [exit 0]
  PASS: --seconds 1, the least: accepted
  $ sh run-timed.sh --seconds 3600 -- sh -c exit 0
    [exit 0]
  PASS: --seconds 3600, the most: accepted
  $ sh run-timed.sh --seconds 5 -- <S>/no-such-command
    err: <S>/cfg/skills/dev-base/scripts/internal/run-timed.sh: line 131: <S>/no-such-command: No such file or directory
    [exit 1]
  PASS: a command that can't be run: the shell's own failure and reason, no time-out
  $ sh run-timed.sh --seconds 5 -- sh -c exit 2
    [exit 2]
  PASS: a command's own exit 2 passes through

=== run-timed.sh: at the limit, the command and every process beneath it are stopped
  $ sh run-timed.sh --seconds 2 -- sh <S>/tree.sh
    [exit 124]
    took 2 s
  PASS: exit 124 after about 2 s, nothing printed of its own
  PASS: the tree wrote four PIDs
  PASS:   ... and none of the four is running: the child and the grandchild were stopped too
  $ sh run-timed.sh --seconds 1 -- sh <S>/stubborn.sh
    [exit 124]
    took 3 s
  PASS: a tree that ignores TERM: exit 124, KILL about 2 s after the limit
  PASS:   ... and none of it is running

=== run-timed.sh: told to stop before the limit
  $ kill -TERM <the runner's PID>: [exit 143]
  PASS: TERM to the runner: exit 143, and none of the command's tree is running
  $ kill -INT <the runner's PID>: [exit 130]
  PASS: INT to the runner: exit 130, and none of the command's tree is running
  $ kill -HUP <the runner's PID>: [exit 129]
  PASS: HUP to the runner: exit 129, and none of the command's tree is running

=== run-timed.sh: without pgrep only the command itself is found
  $ env PATH=<S>/nopgrep /bin/sh run-timed.sh --seconds 1 -- /bin/sh <S>/two.sh
    [exit 124]
  PASS: exit 124; the command stopped, its child left running (the known limit)

